          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Every uniformly continuous map between uniform spaces is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
            (between the underlying
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+map"} Cauchy continuous
            (between the underlying
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+spaces"} Cauchy spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+map"} short
            or even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lipschitz+map"} Lipschitz
            map between metric spaces (or Lipschitz
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
            of uniformly continuous maps is uniformly continuous, as is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            between (quasi)uniform spaces. The composite of two antiuniformly continuous maps is uniformly continuous. Thus uniform spaces are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose morphisms are the uniformly continuous maps as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-category"} category
